1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Inventories of the Orphan Chamber Cape Town Archives Repository, South Africa
2 CONT * Reference no.: MOOC8/41.41
2 CONT * Testator(s):
2 CONT * Jan Christoffel Berrangé
2 CONT * 13 March 1827
2 CONT
2 CONT Inventory of all such property as have been relinquished by the death ab intestato of the '''Reverend Jan Christoffel Berrangé''' on the eleventh day of the month of March in the year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred and twe
2 CONC nty seven for the benefit of his surviving widow '''Cornelia Eliana Serrurier''' on the one and his three children begotten in a former marriage by his deceased wife Mr:s Hester Alida Elisabeth van Boekom named
2 CONT * 1) Elisabeth Hester Berrangé married with Jan Serrurier
2 CONT * 2) Catharina Gerharda Berrangé aged [ ..... ]
2 CONT * 3) Anthonia Maria Berrangé married wih Jan Hendrik Hoffmeyr j:r
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Slaves'''
2 CONT # a male slave named Mei of Mosambique labourer aged 40 years
2 CONT # a male slave named Carolus of this Colony born on the 2 May 1816
2 CONT # a male slave named Christiaan of this Colony born the 9 June 1817 having the leprosy
2 CONT # a male slave named Achilles of this Colony born on the 21:st May 1819
2 CONT # a male slave named Thomas of this Colony born on the 8:th January 1819
2 CONT # a male slave named Simson of this Colony 19 years of age cannot be sold according to the certificate of the Inspector for the Enregisterment of Slaves
2 CONT # a male slave named Jonathan of this Colony 12 years of age
2 CONT # a female slave named Debora of this colony 87 years of age, not to be disposed of the widow and Mr J: Serrurier having agreed to provide for her
2 CONT # a female slave named Mietje of this Colony 43 years of age housemaid, which the widow together with her
2 CONT # children before mentioned Jonathan, Carolus and Thomas requests she may retain by appraisement
2 CONT # a female slave named Sophia of this Colony 41 years of age housemaid, with regard to this slave the widow states that the same has been given to her by her late father with the wish /she being an inheritance of her late
2 CONT # sister Anna Catharina Serrurier/ that she shall not be entitled to dispose of said slave as her property unless for bad conduct and that she in consequence being willing to dispose of said slave in favor of her freedom after her
2 CONC  demise
2 CONT # a female slave named Claartje of this Colony about 20 years of age housemaid being subject to fits with her child Onverwagt born 3 December 1823
2 CONT # a female slave named Pamela of this Colony 12 years of age
