1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Date of death was sent to me by secretary of synagogue where my father had memorial. Burial date given was not the burial, but the date of the monument for the unveiling.  She was in the 1937 Newark directory living with her daugh
2 CONC ter Lena after Isaac died.
2 CONT
2 CONT I write this as Sarah Peseh although it may sound like Pessie because my Jewish name is Sura Peseh and I am named for her, so I am guessing that was her name.  I can't remember where I heard Bailey, but it is listed as her maiden 
2 CONC name on my father's death certificate.  So someone else thought that was her name.  He had previously listed her maiden name as Koddak on his marriage license.  I have never seen her middle name written anywhere.  I surmise that w
2 CONC as her name based on my name.
2 CONT
2 CONT My father gave Jerine as her birthplace.  I have learned that is in Ukraine, near Shpikov and the accurate spelling is Dzhurin.  My mother's family was born in both Shpikov and Dzhurin and we have lists of births, deaths and marri
2 CONC ages from two periods in the 19th century.  I saw Bely and Beeley on Jewish Gen and wrote to the researchers.  I will look at the lists when the translations are complete.  A researcher on ancestry.com has gathered 9000 names of p
2 CONC eople she has found from Ostropol and said that there are many called Biala who changed their name to Bailey.  She has one woman listed as Sura who has a sister named Sophiee and a Penina.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1910 census shows Sarah was born in Russia but the 1930 census shows Poland.  I don't know why, so I listed it as an alternate.  Perhaps it was considered Russian Poland at some point since the jurisdiction kept changed. The 1
2 CONC 930 should be the same couple since since it is Newark, the couple is the right age and the husband is a peddle or rags, as Isaac was.listed in 1910 with all the children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note about residence:  I have been saving US City directories for my father's siblings and always looking for Isaac and Sarah.  8/3/2014 I saved some Newark directories for Lena Silverman, wdw of Max Greengarten and noticed she li
2 CONC ved at 103 Watson with two of their daughters.  I checked Silverman for the same time periods.  I made several discoveries.  Sarah, widow of Isaac lived at the same address on Watson St. in 1937.
2 CONT
2 CONT I also noticed that Alex (and wife Rose) lived at 260 Belmont St. and there was an Isaac Silverman at the same address.  I thought it might be my Uncle Alex and my grandfather.  There were many directory citings for Alex at that a
2 CONC ddress - but when I went back to  look for Isaac at the same address, I couldn't find it again.  I looked for Isaac Silverman in several other directories.  There were many occupations, but I couldn't find peddler.  Then I noticed
2 CONC  there was an address for a "hatter" named Isaac at the same address as the 1910 census.  I remembered seeing several hatters at different addresses.  The 1909 listing for a hatter was at 259 Broome St.  The passenger list when Sa
2 CONC rah came over in December of 1908 says she was going to her husband at 259 Broome St.  I did not anticipate that Isaac was a hatter when the census documents say peddler.  Maybe he switched.  I started a spreadsheet of addresses f
2 CONC or Newark Silvermans with the names of my father's siblings.  I should finish it.  I also plan to go back to the directories and trace the address for the hatter.  I wonder if the address similarites on both the census and passeng
2 CONC er list meet the standard of proof, even though the two census documents say peddler.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spelling of last name is Silberman in both1910 and 1930 census but children used Silverman at various points.
2 CONT .
2 CONT 1910 census shows 14 pregnancies and 10 living children.  All were born in Russia according the the census.   I have listed all 10 with information.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note about Ancestry contact for Ostropol: Deborah Glassman contacted me since I was researching Chodak/Silverman and Ostropol.  She is tracing all Ostropol families to find connections for her own.  She had notes showing a Sura an
2 CONC d a Pesche or Pessya as sisters  from a Biala family.  Some became Baileys or other names and settled in several places, including New Jersey and Canada.  There seem to be two sisters, one is Penina (not Pessya) and the other is S
2 CONC ophie. Sophie married Yankel Rosensaft, also from Ostropol.  Yankel Rosensaft is the uncle that Ruchel (Aunt Rose) was going to according to the passenger manifest.  He was also the person a cousin of Sarah traveling with her was 
2 CONC going to.  (Aside, There was a connection between the man Aunt Rose married (Jacob Gitter) and the Rosensaft family - which appears on the naturalization as witness signature.  Jacob's father, Louis, was the witness.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a contract signed by Max Silverman and  Orlovsky Monument Company showing place of burial in Newark.  Spellings were Isaac and Sarah Silverman. Custer Ave Shule was common name for Cong. Agudath Israel (according to Debor
2 CONC ah Glassman) and I have found that shul in a listing for McClellandt McClelland Cemeteries.  Googling for Agudath Isreal in Newark only brought up Agudath Israel in Caldwell New Jersey (4 mi. away.)  Congregation started in someon
2 CONC e's home with support from Newark Rabbis and community.  Building was completed in 1950's and populated pmarily by Jews from Newark and New York.  It was Conservative at that time.  No information found yet on the nature of the co
2 CONC ngregation in Newark or if it was formally moved.  General histories showed that as members of Newark shules moved to the suburbs, the shules followed them, started by former members.
2 CONT
2 CONT Location of Ostropol
2 CONT Patrosson added this to Isaac Silverman on 9 Jul 2013
2 CONT Ostropol, Ukraine 49'b048' N 27'b034' E 57 mi NW of Vinnytsya (Vinnitsa) Ostropol' [Rus], Ostropil [Ukr], Ostropolia [Yid], Osterpolye, Staryy Ostropil, Staryj Ostropil Ostropol' Novograd-Volynsky Volhynia Russian Empire Near Juri
2 CONC ne and Shpikov
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah died June 30, 1939                hebrew date of death     Tammaz 13, 5699.  She does not have a memorial plaque.
