1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Fall, 2014:   Passenger manifest for Aunt Rose was found as I checked variations of Kodak.  She came as Ruchel Chuzak.  There was a notation referring to her father.  I found that he was on a different page as Aizik Chuziaik and h
2 CONC is birthplace was Altkonstantin.  They were on separate pages likely  becasue men and women were separated.  They were detained as Ruchel Chuzak and "fath"  for special inquiry for medical reasons and the reason given was varicose
2 CONC  veins.  They were tailor and seamstress, going to Mendel/Max at 239 Prince Street.  Closest relative in Ostropoya was Sora / Sora Pesche, verifying Sarah's full name since I am named for her
2 CONT
2 CONT A citation for date of death came from Rodef Sholom synagogue where my father had a window dedicated to his parents and received yahrtzeit notices, which I continue to receive.  Memorial.   Isaac  died September 14, 1934      Hebr
2 CONC ew date of death     Tishri 5, 5695
2 CONT
2 CONT Spelling is Silberman in 1910 and 1930  Census  Isaac has different spellings.  On son Abram's passenger record, he is going to Aizek Silbermann.  .   A researcher on ancestry.com (Deborah Glassman) has gathered over 9000 names of
2 CONC  people she has found from Ostropol and said that there are many called Biala who changed their name to Bailey.  She has one woman listed as Sura who has a sister named Pessie or Peshe and possibly Penina.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1910 census shows Sarah was born in Russia but the 1930 census shows Poland.  I don't know why, so I listed it as an alternate.  Perhaps it was considered Russian Poland at some point since the jurisdiction changed. The 1930 s
2 CONC hould be the same couple since since it is Newark, the couple is the right age and the husband is a peddler of rags as Isaac was.listed in 1910 with all the children.  This occupation differs from the directoriess
2 CONT
2 CONT Spelling of last name is Silberman in both1910 and 1930 census but children used Silverman at various points.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8/3/2014:   The address and occupation are confusing to me.  On both the 1910 and 1930 census, Isaac Silberman's occupation is a peddler of rags.  But there is a 1910 directory which lists Isaac Silverman at the same address as ha
2 CONC tter.  Note about residence:  I have been saving US City directories for my father's siblings and always looking for Isaac and Sarah.  8/3/2014 I saved some Newark directories for Lena Silverman, wdw of Max Greengarten and noticed
2 CONC  she lived at 103 Watson with two of their daughters.  I checked Silverman for the same time periods.  I made several discoveries.  Sarah, widow of Isaac lived at the same address on Watson St. in 1937.
2 CONT
2 CONT I also noticed that Alex (and wife Rose) lived at 260 Belmont St. and there was an Isaac Silverman at the same address.  I thought it might be my Uncle Alex and my grandfather.  There were many directory citings for Alex at that a
2 CONC ddress - but when I went back to  look for Isaac at the same address, I couldn't find it again.  I looked for Isaac Silverman in several other directories.  There were many occupations, but I couldn't find peddler.  Then I noticed
2 CONC  there was an address for a "hatter" named Isaac at the same address as the 1910 census.  I remembered seeing several hatters at different addresses.  The 1909 listing for a hatter was at 259 Broome St.  The passenger list when Sa
2 CONC rah came over in December of 1908 says she was going to her husband at 259 Broome St.  I did not anticipate that Isaac was a hatter when the census documents say peddler.  Maybe he switched.  I started a spreadsheet of addresses f
2 CONC or Newark Silvermans with the names of my father's siblings and traced Isaac for most years as he changed occupations and addresses.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a contract signed by Max Silverman and  Orlovsky Monument Company showing place of burial in Newark.  Spellings were Isaac and Sarah Silverman. Custer Ave Shule was common name for Cong. Agudath Israel, which is listed at
2 CONC  McClelland Cemeteries.  Googling for Agudath Isreal in Newark only brought up Agudath Israel in Caldwell New Jersey (4 mi. away.)  Congregation started in someone's home with support from Newark Rabbis and community.  Building wa
2 CONC s completed in 1950's and populated pmarily by Jews from Newark and New York.  It was Conservative at that time.  No information found yet on the nature of the congregation in Newark or if it was formally moved.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has a memorial plaque in the Johnstown sanctuary (July 13, 2012 email from Cathy McClaren at Beth Sholom synagogue in Johnstown PA) -  After merger from Rodef Sholom.when memorials were taken to new building. )  There was a win
2 CONC dow for Isaac and Sarah, which was given to our family, but after my mother died, I gave it to Phil Eisenberg.  He moved to a condo in Florida sometime later and his wife Edythe didn't remember it.
2 CONT
2 CONT The location in Ukraine is said to be Ostropolya.  I think Selma Wilensky told me that.  Max Silverman documents show Astropolya, but that does not exist in Jewish Genealogy Database.  Closest is Ostropolia or a variation / presen
2 CONC t day Ostropol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Location of Ostropol
2 CONT Patrosson added this to Isaac Silverman on 9 Jul 2013
2 CONT Ostropol, Ukraine 49'b048' N 27'b034' E 57 mi NW of Vinnytsya (Vinnitsa) Ostropol' [Rus], Ostropil [Ukr], Ostropolia [Yid], Osterpolye, Staryy Ostropil, Staryj Ostropil Ostropol' Novograd-Volynsky Volhynia Russian Empire Near Juri
2 CONC ne and Shpikov
2 CONT
2 CONT There are several Silvermans and Silbermans  in Newark directories in 1910s and early 20's that correspond to Isaac and several family names:  Max, Lena, Louis, Alex, Abraham, Samuel.  Some are in occupations related to sales, jun
2 CONC k, peddling, huckster, used furniture, as well as cleaning, which was Max Silverman's business. .  There is an abbreviation "BDS" which means boards.    One address is constant, the others move, but some are different numbers on t
2 CONC he same street.  Max is in dry cleaning, which I understand from Greg Wilensky, was an actual business he had. In two years, Isaac is associated with that business at the same address. By comparing addresses from year to year, I w
2 CONC as able to trace him and several sons from the time they lived with him until they married.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate spelling of Last Name
2 CONT Patrosson added this to Isaac Silverman on 9 Jul 2013
2 CONT 1910 census shows Silberman - So does 1930.
2 CONT Last Name
2 CONT Patrosson added this to Isaac Silverman on 9 Jul 2013
2 CONT The family story is that the name in Russia was Kodak, but it was changed to Silverman when they emigrated to the US. The oldest brother, Max was supposedly the first. A cousin Greg Wilensky (great grandson of Max) found that Max 
2 CONC used Silverman in Scotland before he immigrated. My father Sam's marriage license indicates Koddak is his mother's maiden name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Starokostyantyniv is the name for Isaac's birthplace, written althoristanton or alkoistanton It is 13 mi WNW of Krasyliv and 16 mi ESE of Ostropol
2 CONT
2 CONT 2015:  On Ancestry.com there is a tree of families of Ostropol and Starokonstantinov owned by Deborah Glassman.  She has helped me with information she has gathered.  There are several people from Ostropol named Chuzak/Chudak.  Sh
2 CONC e believes there are two families and that a man named Usher might be Isaac's brother and their father might be Joelik.  Both of them have sons named Joelik and daughters named Leah and changed their name to Silverman when they im
2 CONC migrated.  There is possibly a third brother she has identified.
