1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Census documents and draft registration are available.  Document indicates marriage in July 1904 and Max passage December 1904.  They also indicate age married as 24 and 28.  Therefore birthdates would be 1880 for Esther and 1876 
2 CONC for Max.  Sarah's age on documents show probable conception in 1904 and born in 1905.  1910 census shows Max with family in Newark and Sarah is 4 - Baby Udia never appeared again, but that must be Helen.  I would like to know when
2 CONC  Sarah became Selma.  Boat document may not be Max - it looks like occupation is butler or cutter, and he was going to stay with an Uncle, Max Sacrossy (?)  in New York.  I have notr heard of relatives who came before him and don'
2 CONC t know the name,  but would like to find them if they were here.  Possibly there was a misunderstanding.  I emailed Greg, Max's greatgrandson, regarding discrepancies.  He had sent me the documents about Max and then I searchced A
2 CONC ncestry.   .
2 CONT
2 CONT Most documents indicate Russia.  Draft registration shows Arsterpolo. That does not come up on Russian locations in JewishGen.  Ostropoya / Ostropol comes up and is similar phonetically.  Sarah / Selma told me the family was from 
2 CONC Ostropolye.  The 1942 draft registration also shows his place of employment in Cambria County, which corroborates with my 1st cousin Herman Eisenberg telling me Max lived in Johnstown.
2 CONT
2 CONT The draft registration also shows Max has blue eyes, as does Abram on his.  People often used to ask me where my son Steven got his blue eyes.  I didn't know.before.  My parents took home movies and I have several reels.  There is
2 CONC  one of a Seder at our home in Johnstown around 1949.  Max is there.  There is also a short snip of him when we visited in Sarasots a few years later.  I was hugging him and my father knocked his hat off so his face could be seen.
2 CONT
2 CONT The manifest may not belong to Max.  There is also a discrepancy in when he arrived. Father  Isaac and sister Ruchel came to Max (Mendel) at 239 Prince in August1907.  Wife Esther said she came to sister Ollie in Philadelphia in A
2 CONC oril 1908 and left Max in Glasgow.
