1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Copy document sources in Fact/Source to "All Media." Add other military and "shoebox records." Check canceled checks and bank account. Military papers show birth year earlier than 1910 census indicates. He probably lied about his 
2 CONC age when he joined the Navy since he was under age. He may have said 1899. He also indicated he was born in the USA. he Passenger List from December 1908 and 1910 census both show 8 years old although they are 17 months apart. The
2 CONC  1910 census indicates he was 8, so he would have been born in Russia about 1902. On the census, it looks like his parents year of immigration was 1905 but the children's years are overwritten and may have varied between 1905 to 1
2 CONC 907/9, 5 shildren did not come with Sarah in 1908. Social Security shows 1902 as Sam SIlverman's birth year. That is probably based on 1910 census. I don't really know. Military record shows 1899. There is a WWI draft registration
2 CONC  for Samuel Silverman showing Sara Silverman as mother, both from Newark. It isn't him because he was already in the Navy by Sept. 1918. But it's interesting because both live in Newark. The birth year is 1899 as military records 
2 CONC show, but month and day are February 29 instead of January 4 and occupation is trunkmaker in Philadelphia - Sarah's address is Peshine Ave. I am not sure of the addresses in the city directories for Samuel Silverman in New Jersey 
2 CONC but I am sure in Johnstown from 1922 going forward. He lived at the same address as his sister Annie Eisenberg and also on his own showing his occupation. The next document is a peddler's license in Cambria County (Johnstown, PA.)
2 CONC  in 1922. The story is that he came with his sister Annie when she came with her husband Joseph because she didn't want to leave her family. I did not know she was already married and had two children in Newark with her husband do
2 CONC cumented in the 1920 census. He enlisted in the navy in WWI (Jan 1918) and I have copies of a record that was made for the army in 1942 when he was drafted. There is also a passenger list showing him returning from Bordeaux (could
2 CONC  have been Cherbourg) after discharge from the Navy in 1920 showing he was born in New Jersey in 1902 (although other documents show differently) My father was drafted in WWII and dischaarged in 5 months due to a bill regarding ag
2 CONC e of soldiers. I have paper copies of Navy and Army documents that were not copies of originals. They described facts. I could not find copies of originals online. Apparently the Army could not find actual Navy documents and sent 
2 CONC record of service instead. I have paper copies of some of his army documents Army documents regarding proficiency. The US City directories in Johnstown, PA show a progression of his career from peddler's license to huckster to SS 
2 CONC Produce, buyer and vice president when he became a partner in Walling Produce, which had existed with other owners in earlier directories. My father went to the produce markets in Pittsburgh and met other Jewish people with the sa
2 CONC me occumpation. The story is he saw my mother's picture at the home of one of her family members when he was there for Friday night dinner. He asked to meet her and they married in 1944. He stayed with Walling Produce until he had
2 CONC  a stroke in 1968-69 while I was in graduate school in New York. He was also a partner in a Mountain View Motel in Duncansville, Smithmeyer's truck stop in Cresson, Town House restaurant and bar downtown Johnstown and Mission Inn 
2 CONC Bar and Restaurant also downtown. We went to Miami Beach for the month of February every year and he went to the races. He was also a pinochle player at Jewish War Veterans and some of the ethnic clulbs around Johnstown. He was ko
2 CONC sher all his life. He was also known in the family as the rich uncle and was famous for giving generous gifts. I found cancelled checks going back through the thirties sending money regularly to family, most regularly to Aunt Lena
2 CONC  Greengarten. She may have helped take care of their mother Sarah after their father Isaac died and/or an older brother Avrum who lived at a convalescent home in Newark.
