1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Avram was listed in the 1910 census as living in the home, but I have not been able to find any subsequent documentation. other than references in Newark US City Directories which list both Abram and Abraham.    There is no listin
2 CONC g for 1919.  I wonder if he was in the Army.  My father enlisted in 1918 and was released in 1919 as end of war action.   Herman Eisenberg said he was familiar with the name as a brother Aunt Annie and my father mentioned when the
2 CONC y talked about their family.  There is a picture of My father in his navy uniform with a young man in an army uniform.  It may have been Abram, Louis, or Yalek.  Max was already married with children.  Yalek married before Fagel w
2 CONC as born in 1920.  I'm pretty sure Louis was in the Army.
2 CONT
2 CONT In looking at the linked directories, there ar many linking errors with Eisenberg and Klatman pages linked to Abram.  I'm not sure how that happened, but I will lfix it.  The directories are very interesting.  There are several na
2 CONC mes listed under Silverman and Silberman that could be family names and Max is listed as a dry cleaner.  Greg Wilensky told me that Max had learned the dry cleaning business.  The 1910 census said Abram was a mason, but there are 
2 CONC no listings for masons.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are WWI and WWII draft registrations for Abram and Abaham. In WWII, Sister Lena Greengarten is referred to in WWII registration, so I'm sure that is my uncle.  He states he was a cleaner/dyer, but hadn't worked in 15 years a
2 CONC nd first joint of index finger was missing.  He is 5'6" and weighs only 122 lb.  The WWI registration is for s cleaner/dyer also with a wife named Sarah.  An employer is listed, but I can't read the name or address.  Some letters 
2 CONC in the signatures look very similar. The second is squished, so I can't see the letters clearly.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a 1920 census with an Abraham married to Sarah with 3 children.  Age and birth coincide and this man is a cleaner/dyer.  There is not a later census for the family.  There is a later census for an Abe Silverman who is mar
2 CONC ried and has been in a convalescent hospital for at least 10 yearas.  If this is Abram, that might account for his weighing only 122 lb in 1942 and listing his sister Lena Greengarten as relative...
