1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT First record is on Passenger List December 23, as Udje Silbermann.  Her son Herman told me my father Sam used to call her Udgie and she called him Mitzie.  After I saw the passenger list, I realized Udge was her Yiddish name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spelling of last name in 1920 census after marriage to Joseph Eisenberg was Isenberg.  Sons were Jacob and Morris at that time.  They moved to Johnstown,  where Phillip and Evelyn were born.  In 1930 the census shows Detroit.  In 
2 CONC 1932, Herman and Ruthie were born  in Johnstown.  Several pictures and documents of Joseph Eisenberg's family came from a relatives of a sibling of Joseph Eisenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Joseph was naturalized, wives were naturalized with them.  So Annie is listed on the petition.  Annie's birthdate is listed as March 10, 1896, which is different from any other source.
