1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Mary seems to have been the second sibling married.  She married Meyer Sukoneck and lived in Newark.  Rose was born about 1910 or 1911 and they are probably in the front row of the family photograph.  I have been in touch with mem
2 CONC bers of Meyer's extended family and have seen pictures.  There is a strong family resemblance.  Meyer was a Mason.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1910 census Mary indicated her year of immigration as 1903, but in the same census her family lists their immigration as 1905 or 1907.  She was going to her uncle Yankel/Jacob Rosensaft, the husband of Sarah's sister Sophie
2 CONC .  She was listed as a servant in the manifest, but it wasn't clear that she was with anyone.  The person listed above her was from Odessa (where Max's wife was from,) and someone on the next page was from Ostropol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was not included in the 1910 census with the Silverman/Silberman family.  She lived with "Myer" and the spelling on the census was Sokonik.  They had been married 0 years in April 1910.   I could not find her in the 1920 cens
2 CONC us, but she was in the 1925 state census married to Benjamin Berlin with Rose, Jack and Harold Sukoneck and Benjamin's children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rose was 15 in the 1925 census.  It isn't clear when they moved to Baltimore, but most of the Berlin famly seemed to have been in Baltimore.  Mary and Benjamin had a child together who was Samuel in one census and later became Sey
2 CONC mour.
