1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The  naturalization paper gives arrival as June 22, 1893, but indicates Jacob has been in the US continuously since 1899.   I think his wife Sophie came in 1897 with daughter Annie.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1900 census indicates Jacob was born in 1865 and is 35 and Sophie was born in 1972 and is 28.  Since those are the earliest documents, they are more believable than later census reports.  Jacob's arrival was 1893, as shown on 
2 CONC the report and as documented (in the US for 7 years.  Sophie's arrival was shown as 1897 and she had been in the US for 3 years.  Annie, the oldest child was 9 in 1900 and so born in Russia in 1891.  She was the only child born in
2 CONC  Russia, even though this report says New York.  Sarah was 2 and Morris a few months, so both had been born in NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1910 census, Jacob was 40 (aged 5 years in the 10 years that passed, so birth year was about 1870.  Sophie was 38, so she had the same birth year as she had in 1900.  Anna was listed as born in Russia.  Their arrival years 
2 CONC were the same, 1893 and 1897.  They had 3 more chioldren.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1920 census, their arrival years had slipped.  Jacob was 1897 and Sophie and Annie were 1999.  Ages were 50, 45, 24.  So Jacob was born in 1870 as stated in 1910 and Sophie in 1875, so she aged 7 years in the ten that had l
2 CONC apsed.  Annie would have been born around 1896 instead of 1891 - so a passenger list for Sophie and Annie would be helpful.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1925 city directory, Anna, Jacob and Harry were at the same address.  Morris was at a different address, but had the same business name as Jacob.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1930, Anna, Harry and Charles were still with Jacob and Sophie.  This time they were 62 and 53.  (born 1868 and 1877.)  Anna was 30, giving her a new birth year of 1900.  There is a marriage record of an Anna Rosensaft to a Ber
2 CONC nstein, so it is possible this Anna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sprintza was found as Sprintza Belen Rosensaft, married to Jake /Yankel documented in the birth of their children.  Yankel was the uncle both Aunt Rose and Sarah's cousin Abraham Beilin were going to.  Their graves were found in F
2 CONC ind A Grave and the pictures on Jewishdata.com.  Jacob was listed as Yaakov Shmuel son of Mordechai.  I think Yankel may be a nickname for Yaakov.  (Need to check)
