1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Catharina Anna Grandon de Hochepied (21 May 1767 – 1803) was a Hungarian and Swedish noble. As the wife of the Swedish ambassador in the Ottoman Empire, she became the likely first woman ever to have performed on s
2 CONC tage in Islamic Turkey. Born to the Hungarian count Jan Daniel Grandon de Hochepied, she married Gerhard von Heidenstam, the Swedish ambassador of the Ottoman Empire, in 1783 and moved with him to Istanbul, where they lived. Hedie
2 CONC nstam organized an amateur theatre at the Swedish hotel in the Pera district of the city. In 1786, the theatre opened with the opera L’ecole des Jaloux, the first Italian Opera ever performed in Turkey and, likely, in the Muslim w
2 CONC orld. The music was played by the embassy staff. Catharina Anna participated in the opera, together with a couple of other amateur actresses from the embassy staff's families, in front of three hundred spectators, thereby becoming
2 CONC  perhaps the first woman ever to perform on a public stage in a Muslim country. She was complimented on her performance by members of the audience, which consisted of both foreign diplomats and Muslim nobles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandon de Hochepied, Catharina Anna,  dotter af ungerske grefven Johan Daniel Gr. de H.,  blef 1783 gift med svenske ministern i  Constantinopel Gerhard Johan Balthasar v. Heidenstam.  Heidenstam hade i svenska hotellet i Pera  i
2 CONC nrättat en prydlig theater, på hvilken 1786, för  första gången i Turkiet, uppfördes en italiensk opera:  L’ecole des Jaloux. Orkestern bestod af några  och trettio musikanter under ministerns egen  direktion. Fru v. Heidenstam, e
2 CONC n fru, icke mindre  lysande af snille och smak än hennes herre,  behagade vid detta tillfälle, tillika med flera af  ministerstatens fruntimmer, spela åtskilliga roller,  hvilka till både sång och aktion utfördes på ett  förträffl
2 CONC igt sätt. Spektatörerna voro öfver 300  af corps diplomatique och förnäma turkar, hvilka  sednare ej kunde nog betyga sitt bifall och sin  glädje öfver ett hos dem tillförne alldeles okändt  nöje af så ädel och oskyldig beskaffenh
2 CONC et. –  Både herr och fru H. dogo 1803. 
2 CONT --------------------
