1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=7MuulNymhctoxY%2BbkAewJg&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Adrian Elias Hope in 1867] and [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=q5
2 CONC RMnTffUMNR4dYT5mqkPQ&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Ida Louisa A Duff in 1867]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * April to June 1867: Registration of marriage of Ida Louisa A Duff; in Marylebone (Volume 1a, Page 834)
2 CONT * April to June 1867: Registration of marriage of Adrian Elias Hope; in Marylebone (Volume 1a, Page 834)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.ancestry.co.uk/discoveryui-content/view/6139371:1623 Ancestry: Church of England Marriages and Banns]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * marriage: Monday, 3 June 1867
2 CONT * Ida Louisa Alice Duff, of [4 Cavendish Square, Marylebone, London W1G 0PG 51.516663, -0.1438604], spinster, Peer's daughter, aged 18 [born about 1849]
2 CONT * daughter of James Duff, 6th Earl of Fife, Peer of the Realm
2 CONT * Adrian Elias Hope, of [7 Cavendish Square, Marylebone, London W1G 0PE 51.5169134, -0.1441717], bachelor, Esquire, aged 22 [born about 1845]
2 CONT * son of Adrian John Hope, deceased, Esquire
2 CONT * married at: [https://www.genuki.org.uk/big/eng/MDX/StMarylebone/StAndrew St Andrew's Church, now 21 Great Titchfield Street, Fitzrovia, London W1W 8DS 51.516702, -0.139342], England, after banns according to the Rites and Ceremo
2 CONC nies of the Established Church by licence
2 CONT * ceremony by: Arthur H. Pylaner[?] Morton
2 CONT * witnesses: [5th earl of] Fife; Anne Townshend; Townshend; Charles Barrett; Daliton[?]; A. I[?]. B. Brunsford John[?]; Ericasl[?] Bruce[?]; Arthur Divett Hayton.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=CpwYzmfzmbivUBArPIQzxg&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of death of Adrian E. Hope in 1919]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT October to December 1919: Registration of death of Adrian E. Hope; aged 74 [born about 1845]; in Paddington (Volume 1a, Page 74)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera01byuburk/page/804/mode/1up?view=theater&q=%22Adrian+Elias%22 A genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry of Great Britain and Ireland by Sir Bernard Burke Volume 1
2 CONC  Published 1879 Page 804]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hope of Amsterdam.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adrian Elias Hope, Esq., head and representative of the family of Hope of Amsterdam, born Tuesday, 8 April 1845; married 1867, Lady Ida Duff, daughter of Earl Fife and has by her three daughters. He married 2ndly, 1876 Mildred Hen
2 CONC rietta Scott, eldest daughter of the late Sir Francis Scott, baronet., and has by her a daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage: Adrian John Hope, late Captain, 4th Dragoon Guards, who married Matilda, Countess Rapp, daughter of General Rapp, one of Napoleon's commanders, and died Friday, 18 December 1863, leaving Adrian Elias Hope now head of the 
2 CONC family, and three daughters, one of whom, Henrietta Hope, married Wednesday, 7 November 1866, A. D. Hayter, M.P., eldest son of the Right Hon. Sir W. G. Hayter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms — Az., a chevron or, between three bezants. Crest-broken globe surmounted of a rainbow with clouds at each end ppr. Motto — At spes non fracta [translation: but hope is not broken].
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence — Chesterfield Gardens, W
