1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.zeeuwsarchief.nl/zeeuwse-verhalen/schatten-uit-het-zeeuws-archief/ijs-als-brug-en-ijs-als-barriere-hoe-zeeland-capituleerde-in-1795/
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Hendrik_van_Kinsbergen
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan Hendrik van Kinsbergen (1 May 1735 – 24 May 1819), or Count of Doggersbank, was a Dutch naval officer. Having had a good scientific education, Van Kinbergen was a proponent of fleet modernization and wrote many books about nav
2 CONC al organization, discipline and tactics.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1773, he twice defeated an Ottoman fleet while in Russian service. Returning to the Dutch Republic in 1775, he becam e a Dutch naval hero in 1781, fighting the Royal Navy, and gradually attained the position of commander-in-chi
2 CONC ef as a lieutenant-admiral. When France conquered the Republic in 1795 he was fired by the new revolutionary regime and prevented from becoming Danish commander-in-chief, but the Kingdom of Holland reinstated him in 1806, in the r
2 CONC ank of fleet marshal, and made him a count. He was again degraded by the French Empire in 1810; after the liberation the United Kingdom of the Netherlands in 1814 honoured him with his old rank of lieutenant-admiral.
2 CONT
2 CONT Van Kinsbergen, in his later life a very wealthy man, was also noted for his philanthropy, supporting poor relief, naval education, the arts and the sciences.
